{title: Just a Little Talk With Jesus}
{key: G}
{x_theme: heaven, prayer, testimony}
{x_source: chrd:just_a_little_talk_with_jesus.chrd}

{comment: Verse 1}
[G]I once was lost in sin, but [C]Jesus took me [G]in
And then a little light from heaven filled my [D]soul
It [G]bathed my heart in love, and [C]wrote my name a[G]bove
And [Em]just a little talk with [D]Jesus made me [G]whole[C][G]

{comment: Chorus}
Now let us, [G]have a little talk with Jesus
Let us, [G]tell Him all about our troubles
He will, [D]hear our [A]faintest [D]cry, and He will, [G]answer by and [G7]by
And when you, [C]feel a little prayer wheel turning
You will, [G]know a little fire is burning
You will, [Em]find a little talk with [D]Jesus makes it [G]right

{comment: Verse 2}
Oh, I [C]may have doubts and fears, my [F]eyes be filled with [C]tears
But Jesus is a friend who watches day and [G7]night
I [C]go to Him in prayer, He [F]knows my every [C]care
And [Am]just a little talk with [G7]Jesus makes it [C]right[F][C]
